      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nWidens the module-scope torchcodec import guard in `vllm/multimodal/media/audio.py` to also catch `OSError`, so `vllm serve` starts cleanly even when torchcodec's bundled native library fails to load (e.g. built against a CUDA runtime that is not installed). Fixes #60406.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `vllm serve` no longer dies at import time when `torch.ops.load_library` inside torchcodec raises `OSError`.\n- With torchcodec unavailable, `AudioDecoder` is `None` and `load_audio(backend='auto')` falls back to soundfile/PyAV instead of crashing.\n- The original `OSError` is preserved in `_torchcodec_import_exc` and chained into the deferred `ImportError`, so the real cause is not hidden.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe full vLLM test suite is not runnable in this environment (needs CUDA + full install). I verified with a harness driving the real fixed `audio.py` with heavy deps stubbed and a fake torchcodec whose `decoders/__init__.py` raises `OSError` at import (faithful to the issue): 9/9 checks passed — fixed module imports cleanly, `AudioDecoder` is `None`, the `OSError` is preserved and chained into the deferred `ImportError`, the healthy-torchcodec control is unaffected, and the pre-fix file demonstrably crashes with `OSError` on import.\n\n## Details\n\nRoot cause: torchcodec 0.17.0's bundled native lib (built against CUDA 13) fails inside `torch.ops.load_library`, which raises `OSError` (torch/_ops.py). The existing guard caught only `(ImportError, RuntimeError)`, so the `OSError` propagated and killed the whole `vllm serve` startup path even for text-only serving. The fix is a one-line widening of the except clause plus a comment citing the issue. No new third-party APIs are called; `requirements/cuda.txt` already pins `torchcodec >= 0.14` unbounded, matching the issue's analysis.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** One-line change to an existing guard clause; no new components, no API changes.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** 9/9 harness checks against the real fixed module (see Validation); full suite needs CUDA, noted above.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Minimal diff with a comment explaining the new case.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Summary, issue link, root cause, and validation evidence included above.\n</details>\n",
